At the onset of GI-15.1, the increase in Greenland ice-core δ18O by ~6‰ (Fig. 2b), the decrease of ice-core [Ca2+] by ~ 200 ppb (Supplementary Fig. 3b, c), and the decrease in ISM δ18Oc by ~ 2.7‰ (Fig. 2e, f and Table 1) are comparable to respective changes at the beginning of longer DO events (Fig. 3; Supplementary Fig. 3b, c). Therefore, our comparison of proxy records highlights the uniqueness of δ18Oc over Southeast China with a smaller δ18O depletion during DO-15.1 compared with long DO events (Figs. 2d and3c and Table 1). This scenario is confirmed by another δ18Oc record from Xianyun cave in Southeast China (Figs. 2d and3c and Table 1)52, suggesting that the hydroclimate variability over Southeast China is likely related to the duration of DO events.Table 1
